From f5e5db2a2b33b9e01c86928bd603fef5a4fe19a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:23:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] tests + schema docs for shark_catalog.species
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behavioural tests for the ways a species column quietly corrupts a catalog: the
one-time backfill not running (legacy rows lose a meaning the data always
carried), the backfill running a second time (white shark stamped over rows
deliberately left blank or belonging to another animal), and a species reaching
dwc:scientificName in a way that disagrees with the scientificNameID published
beside it — pinned on the row that actually breaks the pair, scientific_name
NULL with scientific_name_id set and species set, where the fallback name must
travel without the identifier. Also covers the mixed-species round trip that is
the whole point, an export against a database that predates the column, both
directions of the dataset-level default (a per-individual species beats it; an
untaxonomised individual still gets filled by it), and the field's trip through
POST/PATCH /api/admin/catalog, which the db-layer tests cannot see a route drop.

CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md schema blocks record the column, the backfill rule and the
name/identifier pairing, so the next reader does not have to infer any of them
from the ALTER.
