 notes TEXT, created_at TEXT, updated_at TEXT,
 organism_id TEXT UNIQUE (dwc:organismID, stable uuid minted on create),
 scientific_name TEXT, scientific_name_id TEXT (WoRMS AphiaID URI)   -- Phase 1 structure-now
-```
+species TEXT   -- what animal this individual is; NULL = nobody has said
+```
+`species` is added by `init_catalog_dwc_columns()` with a ONE-TIME backfill of
+pre-existing rows to `database.DEFAULT_SPECIES` ('Carcharodon carcharias') — the
+value this app has always meant implicitly. The backfill is fused to the ALTER and
+never re-runs, so a row deliberately left blank (or one belonging to another
+species) is never re-stamped on a later boot. `create_shark` applies the same
+default when the caller passes no species at all; passing `""` stores NULL.
+The DwC export prefers the curated `scientific_name`/`scientific_name_id` pair and
+falls back to `species` (`dwc_adapter._taxon`). The AphiaID is published only
+beside the name it identifies: a fallback to `species` emits no
+`scientificNameID`, because the two curated columns can be written independently
+and an ID beside a name from another column would name a different taxon.
 
